$DATUM Compound BA-tosyl 1 To a stirred solution of compound 15 (2.18 g, 6.42
mmole) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was added with 4-pentyn-1-ol (709 OL, 7.70
mmole), DIEA (1.12 mL, 6.42 mmole), and DMAP (78 mg, 0.642 mmole). After
reacting for 12 hr, CH2Cl2 was removed by reduced pressure and the crude
mixture was directly purified by flash column chromatography. The desired
product compound BA-tosyl 1 (1.31 g, 3.40 mmole, 53%) as a colorless
viscous oil. Rf = 0.2 (EA); 1H NMR (500 MHz, MeOD): δ 8.46 (s, 1H), 8.27
(d, J = 10 Hz, 1H), 8.1 (d, J = 5 Hz, 1H), 7.96 (s, 1H), 7.77 (t, J = 10
Hz, 1H), 7.75 (d, J = 10 Hz, 1H), 7.55 (s, 1H), 7.34 (t, J = 5 Hz, 1H),
4.21 (t, J = 5 Hz, 2H), 2.22 (m, 2H), 2.17 (s, 1H), 1.83 (q, J = 5 Hz,
2H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, MeOD): δ 166.70, 138.82, 138.11, 137.90, 134.11,
131.90, 131.60, 131.23, 129.21, 128.36, 128.15, 124.78, 83.06, 71.04,
70.82, 29.04, 15.37; HRMS (ESI): calcd for C18H17NO6SB [M-H]-: 386.0870,
found: 386.0863.
